cl. 1. P. ध्या॑यति (ep. also ˚ते, or cl. 2. ध्याति; Impv. ध्याहि; Pot. ध्यायात्, Br.; ˚यीत, Up.; perf. दध्यौ, Br. &c.; aor. अ॑ध्यासीत्, Br.; 3. pl. ध्यासुर्, MBh.; fut. ध्यास्यति, ib.; ध्याता, Br.; ind.p. ध्यात्वा, ib.; -ध्याय, MBh.; ध्यायम्, Kathās.)
to think of, imagine, contemplate, meditate on, call to mind, recollect (with or scil. मनसा or ˚सि, चेतसा, धिया, हृदये &c.), Br.; GṛŚrS.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to brood mischief against (acc.), TS.;
 (alone) to be thoughtful or meditative, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to let the head hang down (said of an animal), Car. :
Pass. ध्यायते, to be thought of, &c., ib.;
 Caus. ध्यापयति Gr.:
Desid. दिध्यासते, ŚBr. :
Intens. दाध्यायते, दाध्याति, दाध्येति Gr.
